      ],
      "source": "https://www.bakerneighborhood.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood was first plotted and developed in the 1870s, marking the start of Denver’s South Side.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.bakerneighborhood.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Baker was once known as Denver’s “South Side,” a historically rich enclave that shaped the city’s early growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://denver.citycast.fm/neighborhood-guides/denver-baker-neighborhood-guide"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1930s art‑deco Mayan Theater survived a 1970s demolition threat and remains a landmark of Baker’s cultural heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://denver.citycast.fm/neighborhood-guides/denver-baker-neighborhood-guide"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Baker’s streets are highly walkable, and residents enjoy easy access to mass transit throughout the urban core.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
